# SELinux rules for F-Droid (priv-app).
#
# F-Droid runs as priv_app and uses PackageInstaller via the "package"
# binder service to install/delete packages. In AOSP 11 the SELinux type
# is package_service (carrying the app_api_service attribute), not
# package_installer_service which is the Android 12+ name. Both rules
# below are already implicitly granted via upstream priv_app rules
# (priv_app→app_api_service:service_manager find, plus
# binder_call(appdomain, binderservicedomain)) — kept here as belt-and-
# suspenders so an audit-only run with ro.control_privapp_permissions=
# enforce can't surface denials on the F-Droid install/uninstall path.

allow priv_app package_service:service_manager find;
allow priv_app system_server:binder call;
